// error
// #2998: a call to a runtime-primitive builtin with the wrong number of
// arguments was accepted with no diagnostic at all — `bit check` exited 0 and
// the lowered `rt_call` read whatever was left in the argument register the
// call site never wrote. `osRun(path)` is exactly the stale call site #2399
// found four of, after `osRun`'s signature grew from `(path)` to
// `(path, argv)` in place with no arity check anywhere to catch a straggler.
fn main() {
  osRun("/bin/true")
}
